-- COST-LEVER-Q08-1 (2026-10-26, rem-a4 fork F6, charter pillar cost; agent_issues 1000193 AUTONOMY-FIRST-REROUTE-1 "Portfolio: AI spend above the A9 ceiling" (critical) and 1000192 fleet_budget caps breached (high);
-- it also moves 1000155, the METRIC-TRIGGER on fleet_cost_bound_month_usd, whose arithmetic REM-A5-COST-GATE-1 recorded without changing a value).
-- Card 143 asked the owner to raise the A9 ceiling or cut paid calls, a decision that is not identity-bound, so it is the fleet's. The ceiling is not raised (RULE-8-RETIRED-1: no cap moves to pass a probe).
-- MEASURED (qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 19:00Z to 19:40Z):
--   * cost_usd_30d 343.87 = Workers AI 300.74 + DeepSeek 43.13 (owner-local 242.42 excluded). Workers AI list cost a day: 10-17 15.33, 10-18 39.36, 10-19 55.31, 10-20 45.85, 10-21 22.70 (the burst, 178.55 in five days, research width 24),
--     then 6.33, 5.99, 8.26, 9.58 and 11.05 so far today. The burst stays in the 30-day window until 2026-11-17 to 11-21, so the 30-day figure cannot read 200 before then even at zero spend.
--   * v_cost_forecast bounds the fleet at 852,612 neurons a day = research 360,000 + q08 150,000 + code loop 140 calls x 1,787 + every other worker 92,427: USD 329.21 a month against the owner bound of 300 all-in
--     (COST-SUSTAIN-2, 2026-10-21). 88,518 fewer bounded neurons a day are needed. Per worker over 10-23..10-25 (neurons a day): research-exec 244k (held at its 360k budget since 04:32Z), code-orchestrator 228k, ops 163k,
--     q08 155k, errata-hub 116k (the kimi confirm calls moved to deepseek-first today, ERRATA-CONFIRM-COST-1), paper-reviser 46k.
--   * q08-signal-engine spends its whole 150,000-neuron budget a day and buys the least: q08_gate_pass_rate_7d 0.012 (98.8 percent of runs end gate_failed), q08_neurons_per_published_piece_7d 179,750 against a trigger limit of 6,000,
--     q08_retraction_rate_30d 0.78 (78 percent of the essays published in 30 days were retracted), q08_confirmed_subscribers 0, q08_human_reads_7d 1,387 (trigger floor 50). Research costs 46,737 neurons a publication, code loop calls are the fix engine.
-- LEVER (one, reversible, read by the worker): ops_config q08_daily_neurons 150000 -> 50000. q08Budget (q08-signal-engine 0.33.0, COST-SUSTAIN-2) reads that key each tick and paces the day: spent < budget x ((UTC hour + 1) / 24 + 0.1) gates
-- generate() and auditPublished(); an over-pace tick writes a deferred engine_runs row and waits, so fewer runs a tick and never none (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1: fewer items per tick); no gate, reader panel or fact check changes. A value of 0 disables it (owner override).
-- PREDICTION: q08 neurons on a complete UTC day at most 60,000 from 2026-10-27 (today already holds 140,318 so q08 waits out the rest of 10-26); about 100,000 fewer bounded neurons a day = USD 1.10 a day; v_cost_forecast fleet_cost_bound_month_usd
-- 329.21 -> 296.2 (30 x ((852,612 - 100,000 - 10,000) x 0.011 / 1000 + 1.7048 non-neuron)), inside the owner 300; q08 published pieces about 0.8 -> 0.3 a day at an unchanged pass rate (the pieces it loses are mostly the retracted ones) and
-- q08_human_reads_7d stays above its floor of 50. Revert: restore 150000 (the Rollback line) if q08_human_reads_7d falls under 50 or q08_gate_pass_rate_7d recovers above 0.3 for three days (the gate fix of PR 4835 then makes the budget cheap).
-- NOT DONE, stated: the ceiling of 200 needs more than this lever (the bounded 30-day cost settles near 296); the next lever, if the 7-day read of cost_usd_30d has not turned down by 2026-11-02, is the research budget or the code loop calls, which
-- carry the throughput of papers and of fixes and belong to REM-A5-COST-GATE-1 (control research-daily-neuron-gate, issue 100622). The contract of 1000193 is OUTCOME-BOUND: lever in force, q08 held to its allowance, and cost_usd_30d at or under 200.
-- 1000192: fleet_budget ai_spend:workers-ai 660.09 and metric workers_ai_cost_30d_usd 300.74 are two correct figures of two definitions, not a fault: 660.09 is v_cost_run_rate workers_ai run_rate_30d_7d = 30 x the mean of the last seven complete days
-- (10-19..10-25: 154.02 / 7 = 22.00; qnfo-fleet-control aiSpendCaps, COST-RUN-RATE-2, owner request 2026-10-09) and 300.74 is the 30-day neuron sum (27.64M neurons at 19:01Z) x 0.011 per 1k. The seven-day window holds four burst days, the 30-day window twelve ordinary ones.
-- Only the 5 percent agreement clause of the probe compared them and could pass on a flat spend only; it now compares fleet_budget with v_cost_run_rate (the same quantity). The three cap conditions are unchanged. No cap, target or fleet_budget row is edited.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE ops_config SET value = (SELECT b.value FROM bak_20261026_q08_budget b WHERE b.key = 'q08_daily_neurons'), note = (SELECT b.note FROM bak_20261026_q08_budget b WHERE b.key = 'q08_daily_neurons'), updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE key = 'q08_daily_neurons' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261026_q08_budget b WHERE b.key = 'q08_daily_neurons'); UPDATE remediation_contracts SET verify_probe = (SELECT b.verify_probe FROM bak_20261026_cost_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), action = (SELECT b.action FROM bak_20261026_cost_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), next_due_at = datetime('now') WHERE class IN ('issue-1000192', 'issue-1000193') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261026_cost_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_q08_budget AS
  SELECT key, value, note, updated_at, strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') AS saved_at FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'q08_daily_neurons';

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_cost_contracts AS
  SELECT class, status, verify_probe, action, last_verdict, strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') AS saved_at FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class IN ('issue-1000192', 'issue-1000193');

UPDATE ops_config
   SET value = '50000',
       note = 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1 (rem-a4, 2026-10-26, agent_issues 1000193, 1000192 and 1000155): 150000 -> 50000. q08 gate pass rate 0.012, 179,750 neurons a published piece (trigger limit 6,000), 78 percent of the essays of 30 days retracted; fleet_cost_bound_month_usd 329.21 against the owner 300 needs 88,518 fewer bounded neurons a day, this frees 100,000 (bound 296.2). Paced over the UTC day, fewer runs a tick and never none. Revert: restore 150000 or delete the row (code default 150000); 0 disables the gate (owner override only).',
       updated_at = datetime('now')
 WHERE key = 'q08_daily_neurons' AND value = '150000';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_registry (control, location, kind, guards_against, critical_path, disposition, disposition_state, alternate_path, alternate_tested_at, evidence, issue_id)
VALUES ('q08-daily-neuron-budget',
  'q08-signal-engine q08Budget (COST-SUSTAIN-2, 0.33.0): ops_config q08_daily_neurons, default 150000, paced over the UTC day (spent < budget x ((hour + 1) / 24 + 0.1)) at generate() and auditPublished(); an over-pace tick writes a deferred engine_runs row and waits',
  'cap',
  'q08 spend without a bound: retries and stall retries spent 135k to 288k neurons a day on 2026-10-14..10-20 (owner directive 2026-10-21: research and publication at most USD 300 a month all-in, quality must not drop)',
  0, 'keep', 'applied',
  'ops_config q08_daily_neurons of 0 or below disables the gate (explicit owner override only); deleting the row restores the code default 150000',
  NULL,
  'COST-LEVER-Q08-1 2026-10-26: kept and retuned 150000 -> 50000 on measurement (q08_gate_pass_rate_7d 0.012, q08_neurons_per_published_piece_7d 179,750, q08_retraction_rate_30d 0.78, fleet_cost_bound_month_usd 329.21 against the owner bound 300). It paces the day and never stops it (fewer runs a tick, a deferred engine_runs row when over pace), so it is a lean-mode throttle in the sense of BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1, not a stop. ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE: exercising the alternate removes the only bound on q08 spend, so the fleet does not run it; the paced gate is replayed by q08-signal-engine own tests.',
  1000193);

UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT CAST(value AS REAL) FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''q08_daily_neurons''), 150000) NOT BETWEEN 1 AND 60000 THEN ''lever missing: ops_config q08_daily_neurons is outside 1 to 60000'' WHEN date(''now'', ''-1 day'') >= ''2026-10-27'' AND (SELECT COALESCE(SUM(neurons), 0) FROM ai_call_counters WHERE worker = ''q08-signal-engine'' AND day = date(''now'', ''-1 day'')) > 60000 THEN ''lever not holding: q08 spent '' || CAST(CAST((SELECT SUM(neurons) FROM ai_call_counters WHERE worker = ''q08-signal-engine'' AND day = date(''now'', ''-1 day'')) AS INTEGER) AS TEXT) || '' neurons on the last complete UTC day, allowance 60000'' WHEN CAST((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''cost_usd_30d'') AS REAL) > 200 THEN ''lever in force (q08_daily_neurons '' || (SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''q08_daily_neurons'') || ''), cost_usd_30d = '' || (SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''cost_usd_30d'') || '' USD/30d, above the A9 ceiling 200'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
       action = 'MEASURES the outcome and the lever (COST-LEVER-Q08-1, rem-a4 2026-10-26). Reads ok only when ops_config q08_daily_neurons is set between 1 and 60000 (the lever is in force: set to 50000 on 2026-10-26 from 150000), q08-signal-engine spent at most 60000 neurons on the last complete UTC day (checked from 2026-10-28, the first full day under the new budget) and cost_usd_30d is at or under the A9 ceiling of 200. OUTCOME-BOUND: the 30-day sum holds the 10-17..10-21 burst (178.55 USD of Workers AI) until about 2026-11-17 to 11-21 and the bounded daily spend (about 296 a month after this lever) is above 200, so the ceiling needs a second lever (the research budget or the code loop calls, REM-A5-COST-GATE-1) if the 7-day read has not turned down by 2026-11-02. The ceiling is never raised to pass this probe.',
       next_due_at = datetime('now')
 WHERE class = 'issue-1000193' AND instr(verify_probe, 'q08_daily_neurons') = 0;

UPDATE remediation_contracts
   SET verify_probe = 'WITH caps AS (SELECT node_class, CAST(cap AS REAL) AS cap, CAST(current AS REAL) AS current FROM fleet_budget WHERE node_class IN (''workers'', ''d1_databases'', ''ai_spend:workers-ai'')), rr AS (SELECT run_rate_30d_7d AS v FROM v_cost_run_rate WHERE source_group = ''workers_ai''), flags AS (SELECT MAX(CASE WHEN node_class = ''workers'' AND current > cap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS workers_breach, MAX(CASE WHEN node_class = ''d1_databases'' AND current > cap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS d1_breach, MAX(CASE WHEN node_class = ''ai_spend:workers-ai'' AND current > cap THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS ai_breach, (SELECT current FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''ai_spend:workers-ai'') AS fb_ai, (SELECT v FROM rr) AS rr_ai FROM caps) SELECT ''OK'' AS expected, CASE WHEN workers_breach = 0 AND d1_breach = 0 AND ai_breach = 0 AND ABS(fb_ai / rr_ai - 1) <= 0.02 THEN ''OK'' ELSE ''breach: workers '' || (SELECT current FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''workers'') || ''/'' || (SELECT cap FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''workers'') || '', d1 '' || (SELECT current FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''d1_databases'') || ''/'' || (SELECT cap FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''d1_databases'') || '', workers-ai 7-day run rate x30 '' || fb_ai || ''/'' || (SELECT cap FROM caps WHERE node_class = ''ai_spend:workers-ai'') || '' (v_cost_run_rate '' || COALESCE(rr_ai, ''none'') || '', 30-day sum '' || COALESCE((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''workers_ai_cost_30d_usd''), ''none'') || '')'' END AS observed FROM flags',
       action = 'MEASURES the caps outcome (rem-a4 2026-10-26, COST-LEVER-Q08-1). Reads OK only when workers, d1_databases and ai_spend:workers-ai are each at or under their fleet_budget cap and the fleet_budget workers-ai figure equals v_cost_run_rate (the 7-day run rate x30 it is written from, 2 percent). The earlier agreement clause compared fleet_budget with the 30-day sum (metric workers_ai_cost_30d_usd), two definitions that agree only on a flat spend. OUTCOME-BOUND: workers 36 against 30 and d1 11 against 10 need worker and database retirements (REM-A5 PR 4833 retires qnfo-artifacts), and the workers-ai cap of 95 sits below the owner bound of 300 a month all-in by design, so it can only clear by a recalibration recorded as a fleet_budget migration, never by raising it to pass this probe.',
       next_due_at = datetime('now')
 WHERE class = 'issue-1000192' AND instr(verify_probe, 'v_cost_run_rate') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues
   SET description = COALESCE(description, '') || char(10) || 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1 2026-10-26T19:45Z (rem-a4 fork F6): the ceiling is not raised. Measured: cost_usd_30d 343.87 (Workers AI 300.74, DeepSeek 43.13); the 10-17..10-21 burst is 178.55 USD of Workers AI and stays in the window until about 11-17 to 11-21, so 200 cannot read before then even at zero spend; the configured daily budgets bound the fleet at USD 329.21 a month (852,612 neurons a day) against the owner bound of 300. Lever applied: ops_config q08_daily_neurons 150000 -> 50000, read by q08-signal-engine q08Budget (paced over the UTC day, never none): q08 has a gate pass rate of 0.012, 179,750 neurons a published piece against a trigger limit of 6,000 and 78 percent of its essays retracted. Prediction: about 100,000 fewer bounded neurons a day (USD 1.10), fleet_cost_bound_month_usd 296.2, q08 at most 60,000 neurons on a complete UTC day from 2026-10-27, q08_human_reads_7d above 50. Revert: restore 150000. Second lever if the 7-day read of cost_usd_30d has not turned down by 2026-11-02: the research budget or the code loop calls (REM-A5-COST-GATE-1, issue 100622). The contract is now outcome-bound: lever in force, q08 held to its allowance, cost_usd_30d at or under 200.',
       updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
 WHERE id = 1000193 AND status = 'open' AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues
   SET description = COALESCE(description, '') || char(10) || 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1 2026-10-26T19:45Z (rem-a4 fork F6): HONEST-MEASURE-1 reconciliation. fleet_budget ai_spend:workers-ai 660.09 is v_cost_run_rate workers_ai run_rate_30d_7d, 30 x the mean of the last seven complete days (10-19..10-25: 55.31 + 45.85 + 22.70 + 6.33 + 5.99 + 8.26 + 9.58 = 154.02, 22.00 a day), written hourly by qnfo-fleet-control aiSpendCaps (COST-RUN-RATE-2, owner request 2026-10-09); metric workers_ai_cost_30d_usd 300.74 is the 30-day neuron sum (27.64M at 19:01Z, minus 10k a day free) x 0.011 per 1k. Both are right for their definitions; the window of one holds four burst days and the other twelve ordinary ones; the unit label usd_30d_list_estimate on fleet_budget hides that the ai_spend figures are seven-day run rates. No writer or row is changed; the probe now compares fleet_budget with v_cost_run_rate instead of the 30-day sum. Caps today: workers 36 of 30, d1_databases 11 of 10, ai_spend:workers-ai 660.09 of 95 (the cap of 95, set 2026-09-26, sits below the owner bound of 300 a month all-in, so it clears only by a recorded recalibration, not a raise made to pass a probe). Worker retirement candidates, dependency check read from /fleet-graph/impact 2026-10-26 19:39Z: voice-stt (no repository directory, version unknown, 0 dependents); qnfo-ai-calibration (19 dependents: 10 bindings, 8 scripts) and qnfo-observability (22: 10 bindings, 8 scripts, 3 workflows) are Wave-B merge targets of qnfo-fleet-control and need their bindings moved first; qnfo-backlog-exec is a folded member (no graph node) still counted live in service_registry (kind member); REM-A5 PR 4833 retires qnfo-artifacts. D1 candidates not examined. The contract stays the real measurement of the three caps and is outcome-bound.',
       updated_at = CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
 WHERE id = 1000192 AND status = 'open' AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1') = 0;

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a4-cost',
  'the A9 ceiling is not raised and the card is a fleet decision (it is not identity-bound); the lever must be reversible, read by the worker, and aimed at the spend with the lowest output per dollar, not at research or the code loop which carry papers and fixes',
  'COST-LEVER-Q08-1: ops_config q08_daily_neurons 150000 -> 50000; control q08-daily-neuron-budget registered (keep, alternate not exercisable); contracts issue-1000193 (lever in force, q08 allowance held, cost_usd_30d at or under 200) and issue-1000192 (caps outcome, fleet_budget compared with v_cost_run_rate) re-pointed; notes on both issues',
  'qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 19:00Z to 19:40Z: cost_usd_30d 343.87; Workers AI a day 10-17..10-21 = 178.55 then 6.33, 5.99, 8.26, 9.58; v_cost_forecast bound 852,612 neurons a day = 329.21 a month against 300; q08_gate_pass_rate_7d 0.012, q08_neurons_per_published_piece_7d 179,750, q08_retraction_rate_30d 0.78, q08_human_reads_7d 1,387; ai_call_counters per worker 10-23..10-25; q08-signal-engine q08Budget reads the key (worker.js line 398)',
  'applied by migration', 'one ops_config value, one control_registry row, two contract rows, two issue descriptions; q08 runs fewer a tick and never none, no gate or fact check changes; no fleet_budget cap or target changes',
  'the Rollback line (restores the ops_config value and both contracts from bak_20261026_q08_budget and bak_20261026_cost_contracts); the control row stays as a record',
  'a worker-read budget lever with a measured, falsifiable prediction and a revert condition',
  'fleet_cost_bound_month_usd 329.21 -> 296.2; q08 at most 60,000 neurons on a complete UTC day from 2026-10-27; cost_usd_30d keeps falling from the burst ageing out (about 11-17 to 11-21) and settles near 296 or below; if the 7-day read of cost_usd_30d has not turned down by 2026-11-02 the second lever is the research budget or the code loop calls',
  'none (q08 pieces about 0.8 -> 0.3 a day, mostly retracted ones; q08_human_reads_7d must stay above 50)',
  'D1 reads of ai_call_counters, cost_daily, v_cost_forecast, v_cost_run_rate, metric_registry, analytics_metric_triggers; q08-signal-engine and qnfo-research-exec code reads; fleet-graph impact on four worker candidates'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log d WHERE d.action LIKE 'COST-LEVER-Q08-1:%');
